From 6d60804cd5333073d0d79eaab932d8ba7d84eedb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Solution40 <72304265+Solution40@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 16:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] px5g-mbedtls: add nameConstraints to ca

Allow a CA to be limited to the home network, so a lost CA key cannot
be used to sign certificates for other names:

  px5g ca ... -addext "nameConstraints=[critical,]permitted;DNS:lan,
                       permitted;IP:192.168.0.0/255.255.0.0,excluded;..."

DNS and IP (v4/v6, mask or prefix length) subtrees, OpenSSL syntax.
Not critical unless asked, as mbedtls itself refuses certificates with
a critical nameConstraints extension; px5g reads it with its own
callback. sign refuses names (subjectAltName and a host-name-like CN)
outside the CA's limits, also for CAs made by OpenSSL.
